  "body": "Second half of #887, left open by PR #888 (which fixes the empty parameter list `()` through a pinned `ruststep` commit): when the STEP parser rejects a record, the error CamCraft shows points at the wrong line - one bad entity fails the whole DATA section and the reported position is not the entity that failed (see #887's report for the HOOPS Exchange file).\n\nExpected: the refusal names the entity (its `#id`) or the line that actually failed to parse, so a user can find it in the file.\n\nEvidence: #887 title and body; review of PR #888 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/888#pullrequestreview-5865268790, carried-over note).\n\nDone means: a test with a fixture that has one unparsable entity in the middle of the DATA section asserts the diagnostic names that entity or its line.\n",
